Z||000000||FreakyGT||05-11-2000||02:06 PM||||I have a little prob here...ok a big problem really. I just bought an 87 GT, which had a bad motor in it. I took the motor out and put an 85 GT motor in it. Now it will start up for about 2 seconds and then die! Somebody HEEEEEEELLLLLP! please...while there's some sanity left in me!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiasco||05-11-2000||03:33 PM||||Geez- could be just about anything. I guess it would kinda sound like a fuel supply issue.<BR>Fuel, air, compression, spark-<BR>If all that is aok, it oughta run.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||05-11-2000||03:47 PM||||Disconnect the cold start injector (the wires at the switch) and see if it will still start. It could be running on the CSI.<P>This is what happened when I left the injector connector disconnected.<P>Will it keep running if you feather the throttle?<P>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000003||FreakyGT||05-11-2000||04:00 PM||||The compression and spark plugs are good and it is getting fuel....It will struggle to run when I feather the gas...but still dies. I will try your suggestion Terry....Hopefully it will work!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||05-11-2000||04:03 PM||||Make sure the oil pressure sender is hooked up and working. The ECM runs the fuel pump for about 2sec and then switch in the oil pressure sender takes over and keeps the pump going. Kinda sounds like that could be your problem.||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||05-11-2000||04:04 PM||||It could also be a fuel pump, fliter, or line problem.  It deffinately sounds like it is starving for fuel.  My car did this because it was spraying fuel out of the fuel block (cros threaded flare nut), but then again it was also the first time since august '96 that my car had been cranked!<P>check the fuel system check the fuel system check the fuel system<P>oh yea, also take a looksie at the fuse for the fuel pump!||||reg||1
Z||000006||FreakyGT||05-11-2000||04:11 PM||||I just checked the oil pressure sender...that is what I thought the prob was at first...till I replaced it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> It is still doing the same thing. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Greg Piet||05-11-2000||05:17 PM||||call me wacky but there doesnt seem to be enough info to properly diagnose the problem..<P>Is the car flooding or is it not?<BR>did you check the fuel pressure?<P>There are numerous things that could cause a car to start and then not idle<BR> a bad fuel pump will do this as well as a bad fuel pressure regulator,a bad coolant temp sensor as well as a bad MAP, or a bad TPS,or an IAC, or even a bad cold start injector or a stuck open injector.<BR>I dont know the computer compatabilities, but  is a 87 computer compatable with an 86 motor(im guessing they are peachy)?||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||05-11-2000||07:13 PM||||Did actually see the new motor run before you got it?<P>Fuel pressure falling off. Ignition timing off. ignition module/pickup bad or not connected tight.||||reg||1
